{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtRhr6wKxi4yCkAVEgEt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The system prompt is now split into two cached blocks, so a `save_fact` only rewrites the small facts block. Whether this actually stops the eviction is still open. The `save_fact` path may be just under the model's 1,024-token cache minimum, and I couldn't check that without the API.\n\n**What changed (`bot.py`, `README.md`, new `ANSWER.md`):**\n- Block 1 holds the instructions plus the athlete's stable profile (name, sport, zones, goal, language), with a cache marker. It doesn't change on `save_fact` or across days.\n- Block 2 holds today's date and the facts, with its own marker. It is the only part a memory write touches.\n- The profile moved into block 1 on purpose. Without that, the static block was further under the minimum.\n\nI tested the request structure with a fake LLM, using temp paths so `data/` and `logs/` were untouched. Block 1 stays byte-identical across a `save_fact` and a day change. In a full tool loop, round 2 sends the same block 1 and the new fact appears only in block 2. These tests show the structure is right, not the billing effect.\n\n**Open decision: the 1,024-token minimum.** Anthropic silently ignores a cache marker when the cached prefix is below the model's minimum, and the prefix includes tool definitions. Calibrated against the logged 1,046-token cache, the `save_fact` path (core tools only) comes to about 995 tokens. That is near the threshold, and my error is about the same size as the gap. Options:\n- **Always send all four tool definitions.** That is about 1,140 tokens and clears the minimum. It also stops keyword-driven tool changes from evicting the prefix. I didn't do this because `NOTES.md` says to keep the tool filter.\n- **Keep the filter and check the logs after deploy.** On a round-2 `save_fact` call, `cache_read_input_tokens` should be about 995 and `cache_creation_input_tokens` about 50–70. If `cache_read` is still 0 and creation is about the full prompt, the block is under the minimum, and you need the first option.\n\n**From the colleague's note:** I used the two-block split and kept the facts last. I did not use their token sizes, since they don't match this bot. I also didn't copy the tool-group caveat as a fix. The log shows keyword tool changes evicting the whole prefix (the `plan_week` call wrote 1,305 tokens with 0 read), which is a separate problem from memory writes. `ANSWER.md` has the details.\n\nNothing is committed. Changes are in the working tree only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1087,"cache_read_input_tokens":65756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1087},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d15046ba-b0ba-4e9c-92ef-d295982054d3","uuid":"5c877f19-4dba-4937-a2b5-d6ca4521455a","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:04:14.506Z","request_id":"req_011CgtRhqwGzGB9273mGNBNk"}
